extends /views/templates/layouts/_base

append variables
	- pagetitle = "Chart types | Waterfall"
	- pagedescription = "Waterfall charts in Tablechart: steps between totals, with the totals shown as you wrote them."

block content
	.lane
		.container
			.page-header
				h1 Waterfall
				p.lead Steps between totals.

	+section("Steps and totals")
		p Add #[code data-kind="total"] to a row to make it a total. A total starts at the baseline. The other rows are steps up or down from the running total. A negative number is a step down.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="waterfall")
				figcaption
					b What happened to the crop
					br
					span thousands of apples
				table
					tbody
						each row in [['Picked', '74.5', 'total'], ['Windfalls', '28.2'], ['Bruised', '-16.1'], ['Peelings', '-13.3'], ['Pressed', '73.3', 'total']]
							tr(data-kind=row[2])
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]

	+section("Totals are not calculated")
		p Tablechart shows the total you write. It does not add up the steps. If your numbers are rounded, the total stays as you wrote it. Here the steps add up to 73.3, and the total is 73.4.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="waterfall")
				table
					tbody
						each row in [['Picked', '74.5', 'total'], ['Windfalls', '28.2'], ['Bruised', '-16.1'], ['Peelings', '-13.3'], ['Pressed', '73.4', 'total']]
							tr(data-kind=row[2])
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]

	+section("The closing total")
		p If the last row is a total, it grows from the last connector to the baseline, so it closes the steps before it. The other totals grow from the baseline.

	+section("Below zero")
		p A waterfall can go below zero. The baseline moves up, and steps and totals below it hang down from it.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="waterfall")
				figcaption
					b Result of the year
					br
					span thousands of euros
				table
					tbody
						each row in [['Start', '20', 'total'], ['Write-off', '-35', null], ['Grants', '10', null], ['Costs', '-12', null], ['Result', '-17', 'total']]
							tr(data-kind=row[2])
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]

	+section("Numbers")
		p If a step is tall enough, its number is shown inside it. If not, the number is shown next to it.

	+section("Scale break")
		p If the totals are much taller than the steps, a break in the scale below the steps shows part of the scale smaller, so the steps have room. See #[a(href=url('/features/scale-break.html')) Scale break].

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="waterfall")
				table
					tbody
						each row in [['Picked', '174.5', 'total'], ['Windfalls', '8.2'], ['Bruised', '-6.1'], ['Peelings', '-3.3'], ['Pressed', '173.3', 'total']]
							tr(data-kind=row[2])
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]
				.chart-annotations
					span(data-annotation="axis-break" data-from="20" data-to="160")

	+section("Next")
		p To set the colours of rising steps, falling steps and totals, see #[a(href=url('/styling/colours.html')) Colours].
